{"name":"Lost at Sea","hex":"#8d9ca7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of lose"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having wandered from, or unable to find, the way.","In an unknown location; unable to be found."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lost"},{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Castaway","blocks":[{"text":"A castaway is a person who is cast adrift or ashore. While the situation usually happens after a shipwreck, some people voluntarily stay behind on a desert island, either to evade captors or the world in general. A person may also be left ashore as punishment (marooned)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Rescue_by_seamen_of_USNS_Passumpsic.jpg/330px-Rescue_by_seamen_of_USNS_Passumpsic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castaway","wikidata":"Q508230"},{"title":"List of people who disappeared mysteriously at sea","blocks":[{"text":"Throughout history, people have mysteriously disappeared at sea. The following is a list of known individuals who have mysteriously vanished in open waters, and whose whereabouts remain unknown. In most ocean deaths, bodies are never recovered, but this fact alone does not make their disappearance mysterious. For example, the victims of the RMS Titanic disaster are not considered to have disappeared mysteriously at sea."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_people_who_disappeared_mysteriously_at_sea","wikidata":"Q65070295"},{"title":"Lost at Sea (NCIS)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lost at Sea\" is the fourth episode of the tenth season of the American police procedural drama NCIS, and the 214th episode overall. It originally aired on CBS in the United States on October 23, 2012. The episode is written by Christopher J. Waild and directed by Tony Wharmby, and was seen by 17.78 million viewers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lost_at_Sea_(NCIS)","wikidata":"Q6684359"},{"title":"At Sea","blocks":[{"text":"At Sea is a 2007 American experimental documentary film directed by Peter Hutton. Shot on 16 mm film over the course of three years, it follows the \"birth, life and death\" of a container ship, from its construction in a South Korean dockyard to its travels on the Atlantic Ocean and eventual beaching in Bangladesh, where ship breakers labor for scrap."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/At_Sea","wikidata":"Q137803725"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Desertisland.jpg/500px-Desertisland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Desertisland.jpg/1280px-Desertisland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Desertisland.jpg/500px-Desertisland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Castaways may need to survive on a desert island.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADesertisland.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Robinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg/330px-Robinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Robinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg/330px-Robinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Robinson Crusoe (1719) by Daniel Defoe. Illustration of Crusoe standing over Man Friday after freeing him from the cannibals.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARobinson_Crusoe_and_Man_Friday_Offterdinger.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Diane_Neal_-_Monte-Carlo_Television_Festival.JPG/500px-Diane_Neal_-_Monte-Carlo_Television_Festival.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Diane_Neal_-_Monte-Carlo_Television_Festival.JPG/1280px-Diane_Neal_-_Monte-Carlo_Television_Festival.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Diane_Neal_-_Monte-Carlo_Television_Festival.JPG/500px-Diane_Neal_-_Monte-Carlo_Television_Festival.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Diane Neal guest starred as CGIS Agent Abigail Borin in \"Lost at Sea\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiane_Neal_-_Monte-Carlo_Television_Festival.JPG"}],"sounds":{"lost":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/01/En-uk-lost.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/01/En-uk-lost.ogg/En-uk-lost.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c0/En-ca-lost.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c0/En-ca-lost.ogg/En-ca-lost.ogg.mp3"}],"sea":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/En-uk-sea.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikip